    "headline": "Wind Advisory issued October 15 at 11:41PM MST until October 16 at 2:00PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ",
    "description": "* WHAT...North winds 15 to 25 mph with gusts up to 40 to 45 mph\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...In Arizona, Parker Valley. In California, Chuckwalla\nMountains, Chuckwalla Valley, Imperial County Southeast, Palo Verde\nValley, and Chiriaco Summit.\n\n* WHEN...Until 2 PM MST /2 PM PDT/ Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Difficult driving conditions, especially for larger\nvehicles traveling along roads with crosswinds. Light, unsecured\nobjects may become airborne. Localized channels of blowing dust may\nbriefly lower visibility under one mile and lots of lofted dust may\ncreate poor air quality across the area.",
    "instruction": "A Wind Advisory means that sustained wind speeds of between 30 and 40\nmph are expected, or wind gusts of between 40 and 58 mph. Winds this\nstrong can make driving difficult, especially for high profile\nvehicles.\n\nIn addition, strong winds over desert areas could result in briefly\nlowered visibilities to well under a mile at times in blowing dust or\nblowing sand. Use extra caution.",
